    {
      "id": "COMMON_MESSAGE_145",
      "message_id": 145,
      "file_path": "/COMMON/MESFILE.DK4",
      "commodity": "Cheese",
      "speaker": "Price Info",
      "context": "The player opens the selected commodity’s description in Market Price Info.",
      "english": "Lactic acid bacteria ferment milk, such as cow's or goat's, into cheese. Milk type, bacteria, and aging time affect the flavor.",
      "previous_English": "Cheese is made by \nfermenting milk, such \nas cow or goat milk,\nwith lactic acid bacteria.\nFlavor varies with the milk,\nbacteria, and aging time.",
      "Japanese": "牛乳や山羊の乳などに乳酸菌を加えて発\n酵させたもの。乳の種類、植え付ける菌\nの種類、熟成期間の違いによって風味が\n異なる。",
      "source_meaning": "Milk such as cows’ or goats’ milk is fermented with lactic acid bacteria. The milk, bacteria, and duration of aging affect flavor.",
