    {
      "id": "COMMON_MESSAGE_182",
      "message_id": 182,
      "file_path": "/COMMON/MESFILE.DK4",
      "commodity": "Wool",
      "speaker": "Price Info",
      "context": "The player opens the selected commodity’s description in Market Price Info.",
      "english": "Yarn and wool cloth come from sheep or goat fleece. Wool is warm, absorbent, and springy. Europeans have long worn it in winter.",
      "previous_English": "Sheep or goat fleece is \nspun into yarn or woven \ninto cloth. It is warm, \nabsorbent, and springy. \nWool has long kept Europeans warm \nin winter.",
      "Japanese": "羊や山羊から刈り取った毛。毛糸や毛織\n物の原料。吸湿性・保温性・弾力性に優\nれ、ヨーロッパでは古くから防寒用衣料\nなどに用いられた。",
      "source_meaning": "Sheep and goat fleece provide yarn and woven wool. It retains heat and absorbs moisture and is elastic. It has long been used for warm clothing in Europe.",
      "localization_note": "Keep the two fibers, both textile uses, three properties and the historical use as clothing.",
      "source_reference": {
        "block": 2,
        "offset": 1868,
        "copy_end": 2000,
